Correct me if I am wrong:

To ftp to get pc nethack this is what you do:

At your unix prompt type "ftp grape.ecs.clarkson.edu". Some mumbo
jumbo lines should come up about connecting to grape.... :).

Once your connection is established, it will prompt you for some
user id, type anonymous. It will then prompt you for your password-
type guest. nhack23.arc is in directory /f/uploads. To change
directories type cd /f/uploads, if that doesn't work, type cd \f\uploads.
I forgot which way it goes, but it's the opposite of what it tells you-
understand? :), either way, one of those will work.

Well, once you are in the uploads directory, type get nhack23.arc at the
"ftp>" prompt. You might also want to get the support files, nhacksup.arc(
I think this is the correct spelling of the file name).

NOTE: if you exit out of FTP and do a directory of the files, and they
contain zero bytes, repeat the process, but type binary before you
get "files".

